.* DSPLIBL: the job's library list in search order.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Quartz Systems 2026
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=KINDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=LIBNAME CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIBTYPE CLASS=KINDCL.
:VAR NAME=ASPDEV CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIBTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=LIBS VARS='OPT LIBNAME LIBTYPE ASPDEV LIBTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPLIBL KEYL=KEYS HELP=DSPLIBLH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM BOTSEP=NONE.Display Library List
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATAC.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LIBS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='DSPLIBL/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPLIB LIB(&LIBNAME.)'.5=Display objects in library
:LISTCOL HELP='DSPLIBL/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIBNAME' VAR=LIBNAME USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIBTYPE' VAR=LIBTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ASPDEV' VAR=ASPDEV USAGE=OUTPUT.ASP  Device
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIBTEXT' VAR=LIBTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPLIBLH.Display Library List - Help
:P.The libraries the job searches for an object named without one,
in order: the system part, the product libraries, the current
library and the user part. Type 5 next to a library to see its
objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 leaves the display, F12 goes back one display, F17 and F18
move to the top and the bottom of the list.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIBL/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBNAME'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPDEV'.ASP  Device
:P.The ASP Device of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIBL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display objects in library
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display objects in
library it. The Display Library (DSPLIB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
